          "params": [],
          "returnType": null,
          "description": "Device pixels per logical unit of the textures this pass runs on, passed to every filter. Filters express their parameters in logical units, so a chain on targets allocated at twice the logical size needs 2 here or every effect comes out half as wide. The default is 1 because the textures are the caller's and nothing about them states a density - the same reason Filter.apply documents 1 as the honest answer for a hand-rolled chain."
        },
